<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Ali Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1505">1505</a>–1567</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Shahghali</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Ali was a Chinggisid prince of the Qasim Khanate who served the grand princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. Moscow installed him as Khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazan">Kazan</a> three times, in 1518–1521, 1546 and 1551–1552, but Kazan's nobles rejected him each time; he later led Russian troops in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>. His mausoleum still stands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kasimov">Kasimov</a>.</p></div>
